  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Austal Usa reported federal contract obligations of $348M for FY2026 to date. Austal Usa won 54 awards this fiscal year to date with an average award size of $6.4M. Austal Usa obligations are down 56.9% year over year. Austal Usa received the largest shares of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $195M, and the Department of Defense, which obligated $153M. Austal Usa work in FY2026 to date is concentrated in Ship Building and Repairing, which accounts for $348M. Austal Usa also shows small obligations in several other NAICS markets, including Other Electronic Component Manufacturing at $53.1K and All Other Miscellaneous Fabricated Metal Product Manufacturing at $46.4K. Austal Usa annual obligations have varied over recent fiscal years, including $310M in FY21, $1B in FY22, $428M in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $807M in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Austal Usa's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest FY2026 buyer, obligating $195M. The Department of Defense is the second largest, obligating $153M. These two agencies account for the full $348M in FY2026 obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does Austal Usa sell to the federal government?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is Austal Usa's primary market, totaling $348M in FY2026 obligations. Austal Usa also recorded smaller obligations in several manufacturing NAICS categories, such as Other Electronic Component Manufacturing at $53.1K and All Other Miscellaneous Fabricated Metal Product Manufacturing at $46.4K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Austal Usa make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Austal Usa's federal contract obligations are $348M for FY2026 to date. Austal Usa won 54 awards in the current fiscal year to date and the average award size is $6.4M. Austal Usa obligations are down 56.9% year over year. Prior fiscal-year obligations for Austal Usa were $310M in FY21, $1B in FY22, $428M in FY23, $1.4B in FY24, and $807M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Austal Usa?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense are the top buyers of Austal Usa in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $195M. The Department of Defense obligated $153M."
